WEBVTT

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:06.690
Mikochi, look!

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.110
It's another mystery door!

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.490
Another one?!

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:15.620
We <i>do</i> hear noises above the house sometimes...

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:20.410
Why are all these doors and ladders above our house, anyway?

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.290
They must've been built while the house was being repaired.

00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:25.630
That darn Sen didn't tell us.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.960
We're going to get to the bottom of this.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.460
I refuse to live in a tree full of who-knows-what!

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:33.300
Anybody there?

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:36.050
Yes?

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.730
Who might you be?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.900
Hello. Do you live here?

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.530
Uh, well, yes...

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.740
This is our—

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.610
I'm so sorry! Have I done something wrong?

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:03.120
I-I just moved here. I don't really know the rules you all have in the big city.

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:08.880
Uh, I mean... That is...

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:15.430
If there's anything you need, please don't hesitate to ask. We live right downstairs.

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.970
Oh. O-Okay.

00:01:19.430 --> 00:01:22.180
G-Goodbye...

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:28.310
She was kinda sweet, wasn't she?

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:30.360
I suppose.

00:01:31.070 --> 00:01:32.030
What's this?

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:38.280
The ladder broke off.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.620
Whoa, wait!

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:49.040
C'mon, Mikochi. I'll make sure to catch you.

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.340
No way!

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.550
Then I'll just have to look for something to tie to the ladder.

00:01:56.550 --> 00:01:57.880
Be right back.

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:59.010
Okay.

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.770
I'm thirsty.

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:07.520
How 'bout some juice?

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:10.060
How much is it?

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:13.150
Um, who are you?

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:17.530
I'm runnin' a juice business in this here tree.

00:02:17.530 --> 00:02:18.570
Ah...

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:32.290
Oh, hey! You got down here yourself, huh?

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:35.800
A kindly flying squirrel helped me out.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.840
Want some juice?

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:38.800
Sure.

00:02:39.340 --> 00:02:41.220
Wanna sit down to drink for a bit?

00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.020
This kind of reminds me of home.

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.230
Your hometown was like this?

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:57.240
That's right. There was more going on, though.

00:02:58.190 --> 00:03:01.320
The wind that blew between the branches...

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:03.070
The ocean of green...

00:03:03.070 --> 00:03:04.490
The narrow walkways...

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:08.120
All the new folks that would pop up before I could blink...

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.290
Oh well. I guess I don't mind a bit of liveliness.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.840
Whoa. There are three doors over there, too.

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.180
Hello!

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:23.180
Wow! Yes?

00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:25.010
Who are you?!

00:03:38.990 --> 00:03:40.860
It sure is a lively neighborhood.

00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.280
Maybe I'll take back what I said.

00:03:44.280 --> 00:03:46.620
Oh, yet another ladder.

00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:50.290
I think that's the very top!

00:03:50.290 --> 00:03:51.120
Huh?

00:03:56.670 --> 00:03:58.250
You okay?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.420
J-Just give me a minute...

00:04:00.970 --> 00:04:02.680
Should I give your butt a push?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.640
No! I'm almost there!

00:04:17.570 --> 00:04:19.440
We made it!

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:26.700
The wind feels great!

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.160
What's that?

00:04:32.500 --> 00:04:34.670
There's something here.

00:04:35.330 --> 00:04:36.580
Wine?

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.300
There's even glasses and a corkscrew...

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:43.340
"Congratulations on your new home. From Sen."

00:04:43.340 --> 00:04:44.930
Why'd she stash it here?

00:04:45.550 --> 00:04:46.930
Should we drink it?

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:49.310
Sure, why not?

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:04.450
By the way...

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:11.120
I kinda started living at your place out of nowhere, right?

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:12.700
Pretty much.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.460
I guess I "popped up before you could blink" too, huh?

00:05:21.960 --> 00:05:23.840
I suppose so.

00:05:42.360 --> 00:05:44.740
<i>August 18th.</i>

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.610
<i>Sunny.</i>

00:05:46.610 --> 00:05:53.450
<i>Today, I went out into the city with the first friends I've made since I moved to Makinata.</i>

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.410
<i>Mikochi-san really knows what she's doing.</i>

00:05:56.410 --> 00:06:00.380
<i>She told me about cheap stores and gave me tips for living on my own.</i>

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:07.130
<i>Hakumei-san is friendly, and I really enjoy going to have tea with her.</i>

00:06:08.840 --> 00:06:12.260
<i>It was such a fun day...</i>

00:06:22.230 --> 00:06:23.650
This won't do.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:31.280
I came all the way from the country to Makinata,

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:35.290
so I want to have the metropolitan lifestyle!

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.540
But Makinata isn't really a metropolis—

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:44.170
What kind of lifestyle do you mean, exactly?

00:06:44.170 --> 00:06:46.050
Let me see...

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:50.800
Reading a book while surrounded by one-of-a-kind furnishing

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:54.220
and enjoying a bit of night-harvest Crème de Cassis.

00:06:54.220 --> 00:06:55.560
And on my days off...

00:06:56.270 --> 00:06:59.060
Drinking tea with my friends!

00:07:01.650 --> 00:07:03.730
You're doing that second bit right now.

00:07:04.820 --> 00:07:07.150
Then is your current furniture not to your tastes?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.570
That's putting it mildly!

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:11.780
It isn't refined <i>at all</i>!

00:07:11.780 --> 00:07:15.830
An abundant sense of beauty is the epitome of city life!

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:20.790
Do you want to go look at furniture after this?

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:23.210
O-Oh, yes please!

00:07:28.260 --> 00:07:30.550
Do you know a good place to buy furniture?

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:33.890
I do! It's on Souba Street!

00:07:35.640 --> 00:07:39.930
This is it. The main branch of Multorica Interiors, on Souba Street.

00:07:41.560 --> 00:07:44.150
Oh, welcome!

00:07:44.150 --> 00:07:46.860
Please take your time looking around.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:49.990
What is it you're looking for, Koharu?

00:07:49.990 --> 00:07:51.610
I'm not sure...

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:53.990
Miss?

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:54.870
Yes?

00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:59.250
I want to get a pantry cabinet,
and a bed, and also a chair.

00:07:59.250 --> 00:08:01.330
What style are you looking for, ma'am?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:04.000
Metropolitan things!

00:08:05.210 --> 00:08:07.710
To start with, how about this for a pantry?

00:08:10.340 --> 00:08:14.720
The artist, Kaname, used a compound enamel for the lacquer.

00:08:14.720 --> 00:08:16.600
The glass was made in Shar.

00:08:17.890 --> 00:08:20.350
Ah, how sublime!

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:26.310
Miss, could we take a look at that hanging wall vase?

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:27.770
I'll bring it right over.

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:34.070
Koharu, I can't really recommend this one.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:37.120
Oh, no! What's the matter with it?

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.450
The fit of the drawers and door is too tight.

00:08:41.950 --> 00:08:44.370
And they didn't piece everything together all that well.

00:08:44.710 --> 00:08:48.420
The lacquer is definitely pretty,
so I won't say it's all bad.

00:08:49.630 --> 00:08:52.260
I'll put up with the problems.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:54.130
Here you are.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:56.390
Oh, thank you.

00:08:56.390 --> 00:08:59.050
I also brought a bed while I was at it.

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.930
Huh? That?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:04.390
It's a miniature bed from the Shieko Company.

00:09:04.730 --> 00:09:08.060
I think it will fit any room perfectly.

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:09.650
It's wonderful!

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:13.780
It looks like she's being offered to the gods.

00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:16.490
Is that what you'd call metropolitan?

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:22.120
I've found a wonderful bed, so now...

00:09:22.790 --> 00:09:28.380
For your size, I would recommend a rocking or folding chair.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.130
That chair...

00:09:35.130 --> 00:09:37.930
Oh, you're quite the connoisseur.

00:09:39.510 --> 00:09:43.770
This was once used to furnish a passenger boat.

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:44.980
Really?

00:09:45.890 --> 00:09:51.900
It's old, but it's durable, and the color of the seat is just lovely.

00:09:56.950 --> 00:09:58.490
This here is...

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.660
...really nice, huh?

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:04.910
Yes. It's a bit tall, though...

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:10.000
That pantry and bed from before,
and this chair, please!

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:11.920
Thank you very much.

00:10:17.760 --> 00:10:23.510
Beautiful moss to decorate the pantry,
and the mushroom repurposed as a table.

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:26.270
Ah! Now this is metropolitan!

00:10:26.850 --> 00:10:30.190
Thank you so much for helping me!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:32.610
This has become the room of my dreams!

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:33.610
Sure!

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:35.990
Glad we could be of service.

00:10:37.490 --> 00:10:40.030
Well, come by and have tea again sometime!

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:42.070
I will! Have a good evening!

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.970
Koharu hasn't been showing up, huh?

00:11:04.970 --> 00:11:07.060
I wonder if something happened.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:12.060
Like maybe her chair fell over,
and she can't get out now...

00:11:12.060 --> 00:11:14.570
Or maybe she got caught in the pantry, right?

00:11:19.280 --> 00:11:22.950
Hey, Koharu! You alive?!

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:25.580
No answer.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:28.660
Koharu! We're coming in!

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:37.170
She's—

00:11:39.970 --> 00:11:42.090
It's you two...

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:42.760
You're alive!

00:11:42.760 --> 00:11:45.100
Koharu, are you okay?!

00:11:45.800 --> 00:11:49.060
Some food... please...

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:50.890
I'll go get some right away!

00:11:59.490 --> 00:12:01.900
I've had a wretched few days.

00:12:05.660 --> 00:12:09.410
The handle for the cabinet came off,
and I couldn't get to my food.

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:14.630
And I guess I put my water on the chair when I was cleaning up.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:18.710
When I flew and tried to take a drink, I hit the ceiling.

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.890
When I sleep on the bed,
I have nothing but bad dreams.

00:12:25.300 --> 00:12:29.930
I was on top of the mushroom thinking of home, and I could feel myself fading away.

00:12:35.400 --> 00:12:36.980
I'm sorry, but...

00:12:38.860 --> 00:12:43.820
Will you help me put my room back to how it was?

00:12:45.490 --> 00:12:46.740
Absolutely.

00:12:59.210 --> 00:13:03.420
I suppose this kind of room suits me after all.

00:13:06.050 --> 00:13:07.340
Koharu...

00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:10.510
I'll return the furniture.

00:13:24.280 --> 00:13:25.700
Hakumei-san.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:29.950
Can I ask just one more favor?

00:13:34.040 --> 00:13:36.080
You're sure about this?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:38.830
Yes. Please cut it.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:45.090
Maybe if the day comes when my legs grow longer,

00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:50.850
that's when I'll sit and drink my Crème de Cassis.

00:13:51.510 --> 00:13:55.230
But for now, please make it shorter so I can use it!

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:56.390
Okay.

00:13:58.150 --> 00:13:59.900
About here, right?

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.110
A little bit shorter...

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:04.690
No, longer... Shorter...

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.490
How is it? Comfy?

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.580
It's the best!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.000
I'd love to chat with a sweetheart on this chair.

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.380
There you go again with the big expectations.

00:14:21.380 --> 00:14:24.550
That's right! A metropolitan love...

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:27.420
I'm just positive I can find it!

00:14:27.420 --> 00:14:32.640
Can we go have tea right now?
Please give me lessons in romance!

00:14:33.310 --> 00:14:35.850
What do you mean by "metropolitan love"?

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:54.790
It sure is cold...

00:14:55.450 --> 00:14:58.000
And what am I supposed to wear tomorrow?

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.250
Excuse me...

00:15:01.670 --> 00:15:04.550
Would you like to join us inside?

00:15:06.920 --> 00:15:09.130
I didn't realize I was under your eaves.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:10.880
Thanks for having me in.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:24.770
So you're a traveling cameraman, Mimi?
It's been a long time since I've seen a camera.

00:15:26.400 --> 00:15:29.280
My hometown produces this model.

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:33.410
It's not exactly waterproof, so you're a lifesaver.

00:15:35.530 --> 00:15:38.540
Did you get any good shots in Makinata?

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.750
I got great ones! Want to see?

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.920
Look. I've developed a few already.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.840
Oh, Hakuyo-san's in this one!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:50.380
And here's Sen.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:52.180
Wait...

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.970
None of these have anyone looking at the frame.

00:15:54.970 --> 00:15:56.470
Were you running a secret camera?

00:15:56.470 --> 00:15:58.890
I got everyone's permission!

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:07.270
While camping or working—for days, if I need to—I blend into the background.

00:16:09.400 --> 00:16:12.650
When the subject finally forgets that the camera is there,

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:15.320
that's when you can take a natural picture.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:19.450
I see. That's interesting. It's kinda like fishing!

00:16:19.450 --> 00:16:22.460
So you get it? That makes me happy!

00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:27.090
I wanted to take a few more shots around here, actually,

00:16:27.500 --> 00:16:31.470
but no one in town sells the dry plates I need for the camera.

00:16:32.630 --> 00:16:38.260
I only have one left, so I wouldn't mind getting to the next town soon.

00:16:39.560 --> 00:16:43.690
The weather forecast says the rain won't stop until tomorrow.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.150
Why don't you just stay over tonight?

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.650
There's no way I could impose like that.

00:16:50.650 --> 00:16:54.910
Oh, I know! How about you take a picture of us?

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:57.240
We'll do our best to act natural.

00:16:57.240 --> 00:17:00.290
Well, I wouldn't mind, but...

00:17:07.790 --> 00:17:10.340
What are you doing there, Mikochi?

00:17:11.920 --> 00:17:14.510
I'm cutting up some fresh pickled plum.

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:17.010
I'm going to cook it up with fish.

00:17:17.510 --> 00:17:19.260
I see.

00:17:27.150 --> 00:17:28.560
Thanks for the eye contact.

00:17:28.560 --> 00:17:30.900
Ah, no problem...

00:17:33.320 --> 00:17:35.990
It's hard not to look at the camera, isn't it?

00:17:37.570 --> 00:17:39.160
Hey, Mikochi.

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:43.910
Got any knives that need sharpening?

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:50.670
I do repair services as my job, you see.

00:17:51.250 --> 00:17:53.840
I'm an assistant at a carpenter's guild,

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:56.630
and I also sharpen knives at restaurants.

00:17:56.630 --> 00:17:57.970
Oh?

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:03.310
<i>She's carrying herself so naturally.</i>

00:18:03.310 --> 00:18:07.190
<i>Even with a camera pointed at her,
she's not batting an eyelid!</i>

00:18:07.560 --> 00:18:09.770
That's incredibly unnatural for her.

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:10.940
What?

00:18:11.230 --> 00:18:14.110
She usually has a more carefree way about her.

00:18:14.110 --> 00:18:17.860
And where did you dig up that outfit, exactly?

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:19.660
Spoilsport.

00:18:27.540 --> 00:18:29.710
Thanks for the meal.

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:32.710
Oh man, that was delicious!

00:18:33.340 --> 00:18:38.090
Surely you've eaten all kinds of food on the road, right? Find anything tasty?

00:18:38.430 --> 00:18:40.340
Let me see...

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:42.930
Rice with soy sauce and sake in Arabi.

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:45.930
The bean dishes in Yashiro were also good.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:50.440
You went to Yashiro? It's an interesting place, isn't it?

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:52.150
It sure is.

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:55.570
But some pickpocketers were following me around afterwards.

00:18:55.570 --> 00:18:58.700
Some folks from a traveling caravan helped me with that.

00:18:58.700 --> 00:19:01.530
Do you have a picture of Ol' Emerald Tail?

00:19:01.530 --> 00:19:03.410
Ol' Emerald Tail?

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:07.910
The wolf leader. She helped me out a long time ago.

00:19:08.580 --> 00:19:12.710
Oh. I may have taken a picture. Let's see...

00:19:14.130 --> 00:19:16.630
Is this her?

00:19:16.630 --> 00:19:20.930
Yeah! It's Ol' Emerald Tail! She hasn't changed a bit.

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:25.600
She's a nice lady. She looks scary, though.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:27.430
You said it!

00:19:28.100 --> 00:19:30.560
Oh, that's the barkeep at Kobone.

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:34.190
Lounging about in the afternoons, as usual.

00:19:36.780 --> 00:19:40.650
Since she was free, she made me the rice with soy sauce and sake.

00:19:40.650 --> 00:19:44.200
She's pretty busy in the evenings, though.

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.870
The pictures here are pretty old, huh?

00:19:48.870 --> 00:19:54.210
Oh, those are pictures of my hometown.
I took these when I was a youngster.

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.960
That brings me back.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.630
<i>That girl...</i>

00:20:02.630 --> 00:20:04.220
<i>...looks familiar.</i>

00:20:04.890 --> 00:20:10.230
Don't you start pining for home when you're looking at pictures like these?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:12.940
Sometimes, yeah...

00:20:14.190 --> 00:20:18.780
But sometimes... not so much.

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:28.330
Hakumei, help me carry her to bed.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:29.410
Sure thing.

00:20:38.550 --> 00:20:40.260
Sorry...

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:43.970
Even though you'd been kind to me, I went straight to bed...

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:45.840
Don't worry about it.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:49.510
If you come around this way again, drop on by!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:52.310
Okay. Thanks.

00:20:54.190 --> 00:20:55.770
How'd you like some juice?

00:20:58.270 --> 00:20:59.650
Who are you?

00:21:00.480 --> 00:21:02.490
Oh, I know!

00:21:03.200 --> 00:21:08.370
Mister, will you take a picture of the three of us?

00:21:09.410 --> 00:21:11.200
Will do!

00:21:13.120 --> 00:21:17.330
Hakumei, I don't think a picture like this will be...

00:21:17.330 --> 00:21:18.960
...natural, right?

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:22.420
No. It's just...

00:21:23.050 --> 00:21:25.130
Come on, look at the camera.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:30.220
You can just consider this one picture a failure.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:33.480
I'm gonna take it now.

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.190
Say cheese!

00:21:52.620 --> 00:21:55.210
I sure took some great photos today!

00:21:55.830 --> 00:21:57.370
Mimi-san!

00:21:59.710 --> 00:22:01.710
Your photos are done.

00:22:04.340 --> 00:22:05.760
How are they?

00:22:05.760 --> 00:22:07.970
Good! Perfectly done!

00:22:08.720 --> 00:22:10.930
Could you make another copy of this one?

00:22:11.680 --> 00:22:14.140
I have to send it to some people.

00:22:14.140 --> 00:22:15.350
You got it!

00:22:17.690 --> 00:22:21.110
This is the first time I'm in one of my pictures.

00:22:21.110 --> 00:22:23.150
And oh dear... Am I smiling?

00:22:27.280 --> 00:22:35.370
When the breeze is pleasant, let's eat outside

00:22:35.370 --> 00:22:43.170
The olives are fragrant this time of year

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:47.170
And in the plum-colored sky,

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:51.140
the stars twinkle and shine

00:22:51.140 --> 00:22:55.680
After we take in an easy breath,

00:22:55.680 --> 00:23:00.060
the banquet will begin!

00:23:00.060 --> 00:23:03.650
A freshly-made smoked cheese quiche,

00:23:03.650 --> 00:23:07.400
sockeye salmon wrapped in magnolia leaves

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:11.320
Look, the whole world is rejoicing

00:23:11.320 --> 00:23:16.160
It's itching to dance with us

00:23:16.160 --> 00:23:20.120
And what drink might fit a night like this?

00:23:20.120 --> 00:23:24.090
How about something botanical with pepper in it?

00:23:24.090 --> 00:23:29.380
We could even catch the moon with our tiny hands

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.930
At least, that's how we're feeling
